extends ../../../../../designs/mockup-kit/page.pug

include ../mixins/portal.pug

block title
  | portal — home · UI mockups

//-
  The hallway. Responsive prefixes read the browser's width, not the frame's, so
  the mixins take `view` and write the 3-column or 1-column grid directly.
  Copy and sample data are in src/data/home.mjs.

block content
  +mockHead({ eyebrow: 'portal', title: 'Home', back: true })
    p Almost silent: the #[+code('lilnas.io')] doorplate (no subdomain, no link: this is home), a #[+code('lilnas apps')] heading, and a grid of tiles. Three columns at 1280, one at 390. The tiles rise in 40ms apart. The browser tile is the only one with a status, because the portal only knows the browser's state; it opens the power page, which is the only way to turn it on.

  div(class='vp-scope flex flex-col items-center gap-8')
    +viewportToggle('home-viewport')
    +viewportPanel('desktop')
      each s in states
        +stateRow(s.label + ' · ' + s.caption, { stack: true })(class='w-full')
          +homeScreen('desktop', s.key, apps, empty, failure)
      +frameLabel Desktop · 1280
    +viewportPanel('mobile')
      +stateRow('States', { stack: true })(class='w-full')
        each s in states
          +stateCell(s.label)
            +homeScreen('mobile', s.key, apps, empty, failure)
      +frameLabel Mobile · 390
